A||||7||Johnson's85SE||Steering jiggle||||1||
Z||000000||Johnson's85SE||03-21-2001||04:18 PM||||Hi,<BR> I just picked up the steering wheel puller and lock remover. Can someone please give me a step my step procedure to getting at the four loose bolts that are makeing my sterring wheel wobble. Please Advise,<BR>Thanks,<BR> Chris<BR><P>------------------<BR>If it isn't broke, it's not my car.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fierowrecker||03-21-2001||06:43 PM||||Sounds like you have tilt wheel boogie!<BR>Get a manual!!!!!!!!<BR>If you have never done it, it is a hassle...<BR>I have done 2 so far, and I use a manual each time...<BR>BE SURE TO USE LOC-TITE!!! If you don't, you will do it again in 6 months...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000002||N_Man||03-21-2001||07:21 PM||||your best bet is to get a new column.<P>If you have to do your own column it starts to become VERY complex to get the fourth bolt.  I gave up and got a new (to me) column at pick you part for $30 just had to change the lock cylinder||||reg||1
Z||000003||DXR_DAD||03-21-2001||07:35 PM||||Go to the bottom of this page and click on Ogre's Cave, All the info you need is there!!!.  I'm with N_Man I got a new one<P><BR>DXR_DAD||||reg||11
Z||000004||Will||03-21-2001||08:48 PM||||Once you get everything apart, getting to all four bolts is not hard. There is a special tool you need, or need to fake to get the pivot pins out of the sides of the column. I will find the number of that tool for you this weekend.<P>Other than that, just take it apart and remember where everything goes.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||tgowens||03-22-2001||01:01 AM||||it IS a hassle but I do them here in the shop all the time -- just time consuming......the bottom two bolts can be tightened without removing the tilt mechanism but the top two require complete removal.........I think that you will find that, if you tighten the bottom two snugly, your wheel wobble will be gone.......||||reg||1
Z||000006||Jeff-87||03-22-2001||12:34 PM||||Check out this link.  It has pictures and a detailed explanation of how to do this.  Go to the "articles and troubleshooting" section and then select "illustrated steering column dissassembly".  Very informative. <BR> <A HREF="http://home.t-online.de/home/O_Scholz/fieroidx.html" TARGET=_blank>http://home.t-online.de/home/O_Scholz/fieroidx.html</A> <P>Jeff||||reg||1
Z||000007||theogre||03-22-2001||07:12 PM||||Please. read the article in my cave. The stuff at oliver's has been updated to show the offending bolts. You really don't want to do a half ass job on this. You'll be ripping it apart again in no time if you do. Expect to spand several hours at least doing this. especially if you've never done it before.<P>the article in my cave is also important if you have automatic tranny and decide to just replace the column.<P>the direct link for Oliver's is now <A HREF="http://www.fieros.de" TARGET=_blank>www.fieros.de</A>  Other links, like the one above, may not work, or may expire soon. He's in the middle of reworking the whole mess.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 03-22-2001).]||||reg||1
